260216: ikp_master_264_9c4ea6a3_geri_example

Generated data keeps bit 23 of the payload '0' to mark them
as events.
Timestamp on Crob7 is only generated when no event was seen for 256 ticks
Timestamp encoding is:
   crob_data(7).payload(28 downto 24) <= std_logic_vector(system_timestamp(26 downto 22));
   crob_data(7).payload(23) <= '0';
   crob_data(7).payload(22 downto  1) <= std_logic_vector(system_timestamp(21 downto 0));
   crob_data(7).payload( 0) <= '0';

Bitshift is done to align with bitshift in Xyter Hit data by bit0 = "EM"

